{
  "stage": "473A",
  "title": "OpenWrt 10.1.467-ct vs Stock airOS 8 (10.2.4) QCA988x Xtensa Rate-Control Globals Map",
  "status": "CONFIRMED",
  "attribution": "QCA firmware",
  "live_devices_touched": false,
  "firmware_count_analyzed": 10,
  "architectural_discoveries": {
    "dual_stage_probe_initialization": {
      "status": "CONFIRMED",
      "summary": "Across BOTH OpenWrt 10.1.467-ct (IE 3) and all 9 Ubiquiti 10.2.4 (WA/XC) QCA988x target firmwares, g_rc_probe_period_ms and g_rc_probe_pkt_threshold are initialized in TWO stages: (1) seg[2] (.data) boots with g_rc_probe_period_ms = 256 ms (0x100) and g_rc_probe_pkt_threshold = 64 packets (0x40); (2) when the first peer associates in WMI_PEER_ASSOC_CMDID (guarded by b7_7 peer_count_bit7), the firmware overwrites g_rc_probe_period_ms = 5000 (0x1388 from seg[0] .lit4) and g_rc_probe_pkt_threshold = 32 (via movi.n reg, 32 in seg[3] .text)."
    },
    "openwrt_ct_vs_ubnt_10_2_4_rc_vtable_split": {
      "status": "CONFIRMED",
      "summary": "In Ubiquiti 10.2.4 (WA.v8.7.25, XC.v8.7.25, WA.v8.7.11), the target replaces the QCA988x Mask ROM rate-control module with a RAM-resident implementation (0x0099d2f4..0x0099f56c in PtP) backed by a RAM g_rc_ctx block (0x0040da10..0x0040da84 in WA.v8.7.25 PtP) containing g_default_no_ack_wifi_thr = 3 (+0x04), the 20-entry g_ratectrl_ops_vtable (+0x10..+0x5c), g_rc_per_ceiling = 80 (+0x64), g_default_xretry_per_penalty = 30 (+0x68), and g_rc_rate_max_per_thr = 65 (+0x6c). In OpenWrt 10.1.467-ct (IE 3), boot init at 0x0098845f..0x00988468 calls Mask ROM 0x00947a44(0x004003c0) and 0x0094821c(0x004003cc) via *0x0040940c while keeping the probe struct in RAM seg[2] at 0x0040c240..0x0040c25c."
    }
  },
